// good test case
// Integer division and modulo are total (langref §2.3.1, RISC-V M convention): x / 0 is -1
// and x % 0 is x, so (7 % 0) + (7 / 0) is 6. A back end that leaves i32.div_s or i32.rem_s
// unguarded traps here, and one that returns 0 for both cases exits 7 instead of 6.
// main method return value: 6

class Main () {
    int main() {
        return ((7 % 0) + (7 / 0));
    }
}
